id: pm-h3ipax
title: "GH-741: replace reference-identity service override claiming with an explicit observable contract"
description: "GitHub: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/741. A registered service override that returns ctx.payload executes but is silently treated as unhandled because claim intent is inferred from object reference identity. Define an explicit handled/declined contract or at minimum an actionable warning, align testing/runtime behavior, and repair the first-party starter example."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:extensions","area:sdk",contracts,github-issue
created_at: "2026-07-26T12:46:39.716Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T19:51:32.227Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T19:43:42.033Z"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#de74a49829faaec73e28ece0"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Service override claim intent is explicit and type-safe rather than inferred from reference identity; same-reference pass-through, shallow-copy pass-through, modified results, and explicit decline have documented deterministic outcomes; runtime and SDK testing helpers return matching handled/result/warning envelopes; the first-party starter no longer demonstrates a silent no-op; focused and packed extension-author acceptance passes."
goal: project management = context management
objective: Extension service overrides cannot silently discard a handler result
parent: pm-w7mqzt
resolution: Explicit ServiceOverrideDecision handled/declined envelopes shipped with legacy compatibility.
expected_result: "Service override claim intent is observable, type-safe, and consistent across runtime, test helpers, and scaffolds."
actual_result: "Same-reference results can be explicitly handled, explicit declines remain unhandled, and legacy null/undefined output-format handlers decline deterministically."
